1
00:00:24,541 --> 00:00:25,501
I can see it.

2
00:00:27,961 --> 00:00:29,211
I'm fine.

3
00:00:36,301 --> 00:00:38,931
I can dodge it if I watch closely.

4
00:00:39,011 --> 00:00:42,561
If I don't get hit,
it doesn't matter what weapon he uses.

5
00:00:49,321 --> 00:00:50,651
Yeah!

6
00:00:53,741 --> 00:00:55,151
Nice, kid!

7
00:00:55,241 --> 00:00:56,321
You can do it!

8
00:00:56,411 --> 00:00:58,411
That kid's pretty good!

9
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:00,661
He was able to hit the captain.

10
00:01:00,741 --> 00:01:02,911
Quick guys like him are tough!

11
00:01:03,001 --> 00:01:05,621
This could turn out to be a good fight!

12
00:01:06,671 --> 00:01:10,501
Damn! I can't cut him.
He's wearing chain mail underneath.

13
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:12,091
Too bad, I liked these.

14
00:01:13,961 --> 00:01:17,641
So, you're not afraid of my ax?

15
00:01:17,721 --> 00:01:22,471
You have a lot of guts. You're just like Thors.

16
00:01:24,431 --> 00:01:27,981
You big bastard. Who are you to my father?

17
00:01:29,981 --> 00:01:35,611
He didn't tell you? That's so cold of him.

18
00:01:35,691 --> 00:01:38,911
I heard he's descended from a jarl.
He was of noble origin.

19
00:01:39,911 --> 00:01:42,951
Helga's the one from a family of jarls.

20
00:01:43,041 --> 00:01:45,871
Thors rose through the ranks
because of his skill with the sword.

21
00:01:45,961 --> 00:01:47,121
What?

22
00:01:47,211 --> 00:01:49,381
Do you want to know more?

23
00:01:50,791 --> 00:01:51,631
Do you?

24
00:01:54,301 --> 00:01:56,301
If you want me to tell you,

25
00:01:56,381 --> 00:01:59,891
you'll have to entertain me some more.

26
00:01:59,971 --> 00:02:01,261
All right, Thorfinn?

27
00:02:03,971 --> 00:02:06,271
I can entertain you.

28
00:02:07,271 --> 00:02:10,811
But it's going to be hard holding back enough
to make sure you can still talk.

29
00:02:14,361 --> 00:02:16,401
Do you know what you're saying, kid?

30
00:02:16,491 --> 00:02:17,781
My stomach hurts!

31
00:02:17,861 --> 00:02:19,451
Holding back on the captain? You?

32
00:02:19,531 --> 00:02:21,451
Go easy on us!

33
00:02:21,531 --> 00:02:22,991
You're an idiot! You're an idiot!

34
00:02:28,331 --> 00:02:30,211
Was that funny?

35
00:02:30,291 --> 00:02:33,291
I consider Thorfinn to be a warrior.

36
00:02:33,381 --> 00:02:34,551
Don't laugh!

37
00:02:39,591 --> 00:02:42,931
Thors was stronger than me.

38
00:02:43,011 --> 00:02:46,971
Prove to me that you really are Thors' child,

39
00:02:47,061 --> 00:02:48,351
Thorfinn!

40
00:04:29,951 --> 00:04:33,331
That stupid kid. He came back here to die.

41
00:04:35,121 --> 00:04:37,251
What happened to the prince?

42
00:04:39,251 --> 00:04:41,301
Hey! Over there! Go!

43
00:04:42,301 --> 00:04:44,171
Hold down his leg!

44
00:04:44,261 --> 00:04:45,431
OUT OF THE CRADLE

45
00:04:45,511 --> 00:04:46,591
Do the same over there!

46
00:04:46,681 --> 00:04:50,061
I can hear the sound the of battle nearby.

47
00:04:51,351 --> 00:04:53,771
Stop it already!

48
00:04:55,731 --> 00:04:57,901
Don't you have anything better to do?

49
00:04:59,651 --> 00:05:01,281
Be quiet!

50
00:05:02,281 --> 00:05:03,991
I don't want to open my eyes.

51
00:05:05,031 --> 00:05:06,661
I want to stay asleep...

52
00:05:07,911 --> 00:05:10,581
like this... forever.

53
00:05:12,041 --> 00:05:17,961
Your Highness... Your Highness...
Your Highness Canute.

54
00:05:30,851 --> 00:05:33,471
Ragnar! You're still alive--

55
00:05:42,481 --> 00:05:47,111
This is a dream, isn't it, Ragnar?

56
00:05:49,161 --> 00:05:52,991
Yes. I came to say goodbye.

57
00:05:57,161 --> 00:06:00,461
Are you going? You'll leave me behind?

58
00:06:03,631 --> 00:06:08,591
Are you telling me to live alone in a world like this?

59
00:06:09,801 --> 00:06:11,601
Do you think I can survive?

60
00:06:18,521 --> 00:06:19,901
I...

61
00:06:20,981 --> 00:06:25,651
failed as the person tasked
with your education.

62
00:06:26,651 --> 00:06:31,911
I was supposed to raise you as a jarl.
But I raised you as a normal child,

63
00:06:31,991 --> 00:06:37,451
like a farmer would raise his own child.

64
00:06:38,541 --> 00:06:44,671
Even though I knew that's not what the king wanted.
Please forgive me.

65
00:06:47,631 --> 00:06:54,301
What's wrong with that? You understood my feelings
better than my father, the king!

66
00:07:00,851 --> 00:07:04,311
I never wanted to be born into the royal family.

67
00:07:07,481 --> 00:07:08,901
If I had been...

68
00:07:09,991 --> 00:07:14,241
If I had been born as your son,

69
00:07:14,321 --> 00:07:17,791
everything would have been better.

70
00:07:21,251 --> 00:07:22,791
Your Highness.

71
00:07:22,881 --> 00:07:26,501
I'm so happy, Your Highness.

72
00:07:26,591 --> 00:07:31,221
Don't go. I love you.

73
00:07:44,901 --> 00:07:48,731
There are some things that you only realize
once you've experienced a loss.

74
00:07:48,821 --> 00:07:52,241
You've noticed already.

75
00:07:52,321 --> 00:07:53,161
Ragnar...

76
00:07:53,241 --> 00:07:55,371
I'm just a dream.

77
00:07:55,451 --> 00:07:56,281
Wait...

78
00:07:56,371 --> 00:07:58,661
The time for you to awake has come.

79
00:07:58,741 --> 00:08:01,121
No... Ragnar!

80
00:08:01,211 --> 00:08:02,461
Come back!

81
00:08:03,671 --> 00:08:04,501
Come back!

82
00:08:07,421 --> 00:08:10,801
I wish you well, Your Highness.

83
00:08:16,091 --> 00:08:17,181
Ragnar...

84
00:08:35,861 --> 00:08:38,581
Don't be afraid! Attack together!

85
00:08:46,421 --> 00:08:49,501
Are you hurt anywhere?

86
00:08:53,591 --> 00:08:58,351
Those men are fighting over you.

87
00:08:58,431 --> 00:09:01,181
The winner is going to take you.

88
00:09:04,181 --> 00:09:07,981
You're a priest. Aren't you going
to stop them from fighting?

89
00:09:09,021 --> 00:09:14,571
Is there a way to stop them? It's better
to let those who wish to die, die.

90
00:09:23,581 --> 00:09:24,911
I had a dream.

91
00:09:26,041 --> 00:09:27,541
It was a dream about Ragnar.

92
00:09:28,961 --> 00:09:30,501
He said goodbye.

93
00:09:31,631 --> 00:09:33,711
He was a faithful man, even in death.

94
00:09:38,221 --> 00:09:39,931
In this world...

95
00:09:41,011 --> 00:09:44,061
there's no one who loves me anymore.

96
00:09:47,351 --> 00:09:52,401
You've found enlightenment. But you're wrong.

97
00:09:53,821 --> 00:09:58,071
Was the emotion that Ragnar felt towards you love?

98
00:09:59,531 --> 00:10:02,121
In order to keep you safe,

99
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:05,411
he watched as 62 innocent villagers were killed.

100
00:10:08,171 --> 00:10:09,791
Your Highness.

101
00:10:09,881 --> 00:10:11,291
Love...

102
00:10:11,381 --> 00:10:12,541
What is it?

103
00:10:16,011 --> 00:10:19,761
But you know, these guys weren't that good.

104
00:10:19,841 --> 00:10:23,311
It's not easy to find strong opponents.

105
00:10:23,391 --> 00:10:26,221
We'll never get to Valhalla.

106
00:10:29,351 --> 00:10:31,361
Is the captain's duel still going on?

107
00:10:31,441 --> 00:10:33,441
No way. He should have killed him instantly.

108
00:10:33,521 --> 00:10:35,981
Then what are they so excited about?

109
00:10:37,741 --> 00:10:39,031
I'll go check.

110
00:10:39,111 --> 00:10:40,071
Me too.

111
00:10:40,161 --> 00:10:41,661
Hey! What's going on?

112
00:10:43,911 --> 00:10:44,871
Kill him!

113
00:10:44,951 --> 00:10:45,791
Captain!

114
00:10:45,871 --> 00:10:46,911
You kid!

115
00:10:47,001 --> 00:10:48,161
Stop running away!

116
00:10:59,381 --> 00:11:00,471
Impossible!

117
00:11:00,551 --> 00:11:02,471
How could the captain...?

118
00:11:02,551 --> 00:11:06,221
He's getting beaten up by that kid!

119
00:11:06,311 --> 00:11:08,681
Nice, Thorfinn!

120
00:11:08,771 --> 00:11:13,061
I don't even have five men who'd be a match for you!

121
00:11:16,151 --> 00:11:18,781
It's the same chain mail as before.

122
00:11:18,861 --> 00:11:21,241
I should aim for tendons in his arms and legs.

123
00:11:22,241 --> 00:11:26,121
I tried to go after his vitals in London,
and I paid the price.

124
00:11:26,201 --> 00:11:28,951
I can deliver the final blow once I stop him from moving.

125
00:11:29,961 --> 00:11:34,881
However, I know you're strong,
but your swordsmanship

126
00:11:34,961 --> 00:11:37,961
is, well, only average.

127
00:11:39,211 --> 00:11:42,761
There's still something missing
before you achieve perfection as a warrior.

128
00:11:44,971 --> 00:11:48,391
If that's the case, then,
why are you having a hard time?

129
00:11:48,471 --> 00:11:50,021
Good point.

130
00:11:50,101 --> 00:11:51,941
I'm missing something, too.

131
00:11:52,021 --> 00:11:56,361
I thought perhaps I could learn it from you,
since you're Thors' child.

132
00:11:58,731 --> 00:12:01,151
Hey, Thorfinn.

133
00:12:01,241 --> 00:12:02,741
What do you think?

134
00:12:06,741 --> 00:12:08,621
What does it mean

135
00:12:09,621 --> 00:12:10,581
to be a true warrior?

136
00:12:18,881 --> 00:12:21,671
Are you asking what love is?

137
00:12:23,221 --> 00:12:26,471
Are you saying that Ragnar didn't love me?

138
00:12:28,051 --> 00:12:28,971
Yes.

139
00:12:30,641 --> 00:12:32,681
Then let me ask you.

140
00:12:33,731 --> 00:12:35,941
If what Ragnar felt wasn't love,

141
00:12:36,021 --> 00:12:39,231
then who can embody love correctly?

142
00:12:40,731 --> 00:12:42,441
He's right there.

143
00:12:43,451 --> 00:12:44,321
See?

144
00:12:49,411 --> 00:12:55,501
When he died, he became more beautiful
than anyone among the living.

145
00:12:55,581 --> 00:12:57,711
He's love itself.

146
00:13:00,171 --> 00:13:05,431
He'll never hate others or steal anymore.

147
00:13:06,721 --> 00:13:09,931
He was abandoned there.

148
00:13:10,011 --> 00:13:14,681
He's going to give his body with generosity
to the beasts and the insects.

149
00:13:16,061 --> 00:13:19,191
He lies exposed to the wind and the rain,

150
00:13:19,271 --> 00:13:22,441
but won't speak a single word in complaint.

151
00:13:25,071 --> 00:13:26,151
Death...

152
00:13:27,491 --> 00:13:30,161
perfects a person.

153
00:13:38,541 --> 00:13:39,381
Hey!

154
00:13:39,461 --> 00:13:41,211
Do it! Come on!

155
00:13:43,631 --> 00:13:45,091
Damn!

156
00:13:45,171 --> 00:13:47,091
So, you don't know?

157
00:13:47,181 --> 00:13:50,301
Don't worry about it.
I wasn't expecting you to know anyway.

158
00:13:51,601 --> 00:13:53,391
That was dirty!

159
00:13:59,231 --> 00:14:03,021
Are you saying that death is the essence of love?

160
00:14:05,111 --> 00:14:06,111
Yes.

161
00:14:07,111 --> 00:14:11,241
Then what is the feeling when parents
care for their children,

162
00:14:11,321 --> 00:14:15,871
when a husband and wife care for each other,
and when Ragnar cares about me?

163
00:14:15,951 --> 00:14:18,331
It's discrimination.

164
00:14:18,421 --> 00:14:23,131
It's no different from fawning over a king
while hitting a slave with a whip.

165
00:14:24,591 --> 00:14:30,591
To Ragnar, you were more important
than anyone else, Your Highness.

166
00:14:31,601 --> 00:14:34,811
Probably even more important than his own life.

167
00:14:37,021 --> 00:14:43,611
His tender feelings towards you were discrimination.

168
00:14:51,951 --> 00:14:53,201
I see.

169
00:14:55,491 --> 00:14:56,831
I'm beginning to understand.

170
00:15:00,331 --> 00:15:02,211
I feel like

171
00:15:02,291 --> 00:15:04,421
the fog has lifted.

172
00:15:10,131 --> 00:15:11,551
What?

173
00:15:11,641 --> 00:15:13,221
Come on!

174
00:15:13,301 --> 00:15:14,431
He's done with you!

175
00:15:15,891 --> 00:15:16,891
Hey...

176
00:15:25,901 --> 00:15:28,321
Damn... It's still too shallow.

177
00:15:33,781 --> 00:15:35,451
I'm beginning to understand.

178
00:15:35,531 --> 00:15:36,911
This snow...

179
00:15:38,661 --> 00:15:40,461
is love, right?

180
00:15:41,751 --> 00:15:43,211
That's right.

181
00:15:47,211 --> 00:15:48,461
The sky.

182
00:15:49,801 --> 00:15:51,171
The sun.

183
00:15:52,181 --> 00:15:54,051
The wind.

184
00:15:54,141 --> 00:15:54,971
The fog.

185
00:15:56,101 --> 00:15:57,261
The mountains.

186
00:16:02,391 --> 00:16:03,401
But then...

187
00:16:07,651 --> 00:16:08,981
I can't believe it.

188
00:16:09,981 --> 00:16:11,031
The world.

189
00:16:12,031 --> 00:16:15,411
The creation of God is so beautiful.
But then why...

190
00:16:19,081 --> 00:16:20,911
is there no love...

191
00:16:22,461 --> 00:16:23,921
in the hearts of men?

192
00:16:32,051 --> 00:16:35,761
They say that the reason we turned into
creatures like this

193
00:16:37,101 --> 00:16:40,311
is because our ancestors disobeyed God

194
00:16:40,391 --> 00:16:44,061
and committed a sin long ago.

195
00:16:46,021 --> 00:16:47,361
We were...

196
00:16:48,651 --> 00:16:51,571
expelled from paradise.

197
00:17:05,461 --> 00:17:06,291
What?

198
00:17:06,371 --> 00:17:07,711
Where did he go?

199
00:17:08,921 --> 00:17:10,751
Hey. What's that?

200
00:17:10,841 --> 00:17:15,131
He dampened the shock with his legs. Nice move.

201
00:17:25,311 --> 00:17:26,191
Over there!

202
00:17:26,271 --> 00:17:27,811
Wow!

203
00:17:27,901 --> 00:17:29,021
He must be dead now!

204
00:17:29,111 --> 00:17:31,111
Impressive, captain!

205
00:17:32,901 --> 00:17:34,151
Damn.

206
00:17:35,201 --> 00:17:37,611
I've lost all hope now.

207
00:18:05,771 --> 00:18:07,811
It looks like the battle is over.

208
00:18:09,191 --> 00:18:10,901
But

209
00:18:10,981 --> 00:18:15,321
this is no good. That man has gone insane.

210
00:18:17,031 --> 00:18:20,071
Your Highness. You had better run away.

211
00:18:25,201 --> 00:18:26,371
Sane?

212
00:18:28,001 --> 00:18:31,751
Is anyone sane in this world?

213
00:18:34,921 --> 00:18:36,301
Everyone's the same.

214
00:18:37,471 --> 00:18:38,801
Everyone's the same.

215
00:18:40,131 --> 00:18:44,181
No one knows how to love.

216
00:18:45,311 --> 00:18:47,271
No one knows the meaning of life.

217
00:18:47,351 --> 00:18:49,101
No one knows the meaning of death.

218
00:18:50,101 --> 00:18:52,651
No one even knows the reason they're fighting.

219
00:18:54,231 --> 00:18:55,321
Your Highness.

220
00:19:01,821 --> 00:19:04,911
I've had enough. I'm sick of it.

221
00:19:18,671 --> 00:19:22,551
What we lost in exchange for wisdom...

222
00:19:22,641 --> 00:19:26,931
The most important thing... It's something

223
00:19:27,021 --> 00:19:31,101
that we'll never get back as long as we live.

224
00:19:36,191 --> 00:19:37,651
We'll never attain it.

225
00:19:38,651 --> 00:19:40,321
Yet, even then...

226
00:19:40,401 --> 00:19:42,911
You still tell us to seek it?

227
00:19:44,161 --> 00:19:45,661
Father in heaven!

228
00:19:57,841 --> 00:19:59,921
Miserable warrior.

229
00:20:00,011 --> 00:20:02,011
You're the farthest from love.

230
00:20:03,091 --> 00:20:05,011
You, who have been expelled from paradise.

231
00:20:13,311 --> 00:20:18,361
Isn't there any way to end the suffering
from your punishment other than death?

232
00:20:20,861 --> 00:20:26,241
Are you saying that we only exist
so that we may be tested and endure?

233
00:20:26,321 --> 00:20:28,201
Father in heaven!

234
00:20:28,281 --> 00:20:32,461
This man's soul cannot be saved
through the trials you set for him!

235
00:20:55,651 --> 00:20:56,691
Father.

236
00:20:57,691 --> 00:20:59,861
I no longer seek your salvation.

237
00:21:00,861 --> 00:21:03,151
If you will no longer give us salvation,

238
00:21:03,241 --> 00:21:05,031
then, with our own hands,

239
00:21:05,111 --> 00:21:06,991
on this earth,

240
00:21:07,071 --> 00:21:08,871
we shall create our own paradise.

241
00:21:13,081 --> 00:21:15,291
What? Prince?

242
00:21:22,381 --> 00:21:23,761
Ow!

243
00:21:23,841 --> 00:21:25,681
Prince! Are you okay?

244
00:21:27,511 --> 00:21:29,641
Stop, you fools.

245
00:21:29,721 --> 00:21:31,931
Don't fight futile battles anymore.

246
00:21:32,021 --> 00:21:33,931
Futile?

247
00:21:36,771 --> 00:21:38,941
Your wounds are deep. Are you okay?

248
00:21:39,021 --> 00:21:42,821
Damn. I slipped up.

249
00:21:42,901 --> 00:21:46,361
Don't move. Your stomach is cut. Willibald!

250
00:21:48,411 --> 00:21:50,491
Treat his wounds.

251
00:21:50,581 --> 00:21:52,411
I'm going to catch the horses.

252
00:21:53,451 --> 00:21:54,951
You. Help him.

253
00:21:56,161 --> 00:22:00,461
Your Highness, I've seen a miracle.

254
00:22:00,541 --> 00:22:02,341
Be quiet and treat his wounds.

255
00:22:02,421 --> 00:22:06,721
Hey! Prince! Where are you going?

256
00:22:06,801 --> 00:22:12,061
We're going to give you to Thorkell!
Or else my buddies--

257
00:22:12,141 --> 00:22:14,521
I was already planning to see Thorkell.

258
00:22:15,521 --> 00:22:19,231
We won't be able to transport the wounded
unless we borrow their sleds.

259
00:22:19,311 --> 00:22:23,361
What? You're talking nonsense!

260
00:22:23,441 --> 00:22:27,201
Do you have any idea why I'm in
such a mess right now? You idiot!

261
00:22:27,281 --> 00:22:31,321
If you get captured by Thorkell,
then there will be no meaning to any of this!

262
00:22:32,741 --> 00:22:33,871
Meaning?

263
00:22:33,951 --> 00:22:35,581
Did you say meaning?

264
00:22:35,661 --> 00:22:37,961
The meaning of your battles?

265
00:22:41,791 --> 00:22:44,341
There is no meaning to a battle like this.

266
00:22:45,341 --> 00:22:46,841
So, don't die.

267
00:22:48,671 --> 00:22:51,841
Warriors. Become my vassals.

268
00:22:51,931 --> 00:22:56,021
I shall teach you about when you must fight,
and against whom.

269
00:22:57,311 --> 00:23:02,561
I shall give meaning to your battles.
To your life and death.

270
00:23:05,151 --> 00:23:05,981
That's what...

271
